---
description: Format method chains with one call per line when chain has two or more calls
globs: "**/*.{js,ts,vue}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Chained calls formatting

When a chain has **two or more** chained calls (two or more dots), put each call on its own line. Use tabs for indentation (project standard).

**Wrong (long chain on one line):**
```ts
customRenderer(MyView).withRoute('/').withProps({ id: 1 }).build();
```

**Wrong (multiple chained calls on same line after break):**
```ts
customRenderer(MyView).withRoute('/')
	.withProps({ id: 1 }).build();
```

**Correct (one call per line, tabs):**
```ts
customRenderer(MyView)
	.withRoute('/')
	.withProps({ id: 1 })
	.build();
```

**Correct (single chained call may stay on one line):**
```ts
expect(MyView).toBeVisible();
```

Single calls like `foo()` and chains with exactly one dot (e.g. `a().b()`) may stay on one line. Enforced by ESLint `@stylistic/newline-per-chained-call` with `ignoreChainWithDepth: 1`.
